From 9bd76806f0b4b1a45413982f1e9075d6a00ff262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:50:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dock: Launches on a double-click, with Window Maker's dots
 and launching look.

As Window Maker's docked icons:

* Launchers launch on a double-click; with `SingleClickLaunch = Yes` in
  the configuration, on a click (as before). The double-click time is
  `Mouse.DoubleClickTime`. A double-click on the launcher of a running
  application shows it instead: Its windows are restored, the workspace of
  one of them becomes the current one, and it is raised and activated.
* A launcher whose application is not running shows three dots at its
  lower left (make3Dots), instead of the "Running" label when it runs.
* While launching, until a window of the `AppID` shows up (at most 10 s),
  the launcher is stippled.
* `AutoLaunch = Yes` in a launcher starts it when `wlmdock` starts: "Start
  when Window Maker is started".

Documents `SingleClickLaunch` and `DockSettingsCommand` in Config.plist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
